# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF, on every
# platform.
#
# The line endings were once blamed for a CI failure: the scheduler
# vectors were committed with CRLF (the machine that wrote them runs
# Windows) while the CI writes them with LF, so the comparison failed
# on the line endings alone. That was NOT the cause. The cause was
# that simulation/expected_vectors.json was gitignored, and `git diff`
# on an untracked file exits 0 -- so the drift check never fired at
# all, whatever the line endings were. The file is tracked now, and
# the normalisation below is kept because it makes the comparison
# meaningful rather than noisy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vectors and the schema are generated artefacts: they must not be
# touched by a merge driver.
android/app/src/test/resources/srs_vectors.json -diff
simulation/expected_vectors.json -diff
android/app/schemas/**/*.json -diff

# The Windows batch file needs CRLF: cmd.exe does not run a .bat file
# whose lines end with a bare LF.
android/gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
